From 195060ba4db5715ce71cce1e713df289078b924c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: packetloss404 <packetloss404@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 08:15:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] config: validate settings at boot and name the missing
 variable

A missing env_from variable, an api_key_env naming an unset variable, a
custom provider with an unusable base_url, an enabled MCP server with no
command, an out-of-range behavior value, and a default provider with no
key were each reported somewhere -- but each somewhere else, and some
only when the feature was first used. Config.ValidationProblems produces
one list from the loaded config; the TUI, run, and acp print it to
stderr at startup, and doctor carries it as config.validation.

Reported, never fatal, the same way CompatProblems is: this is a file a
person typed. Anything already fatal (permission policy, Sugar/Conduit
ranges) still fails where it did. acp also gains the .env and compat
reports the TUI and run already printed.

Audit patch P08 (dark-period hardening). Rollback: git revert this
commit; no on-disk format changes. New exported symbol:
(*config.Config).ValidationProblems; callers are main.go run(),
run_command.go, acp.go, doctor.go.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
